From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:12:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: make an off-region block read fail attributably

Level#getCurrentWorldData() returns null when the calling thread is not ticking
a region of that world, and Level#getBlockStateIfLoaded dereferences it with no
null check. A cross-region block read therefore does not end in
TickThread.ensureTickThread's message - which carries thread context, world and
position, and logs a stack trace - but in

  NullPointerException: Cannot read field "captureTreeGeneration"
    because the return value of "Level.getCurrentWorldData()" is null

naming a field that has nothing to do with the problem. Measured: 26 of them in
one soak run, all from CraftWorld#rayTraceBlocks called off-region, and working
out what they meant needed a separate investigation.

This fork's model is "let it load, then fail loudly at the real callsite", and
that only works if the failure can be attributed. Nothing about the outcome
changes: the read already failed and still fails, at the same place, for the
same reason - only the exception's identity and diagnostics change. Same pure
diagnostics category as patch 0024's runtime access guard.

This adds the helper the Level hook calls. Scope is getBlockStateIfLoaded, the
one path with measured evidence; other getCurrentWorldData() dereferences have
the same shape but no observed occurrence.

Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.regionReadDiagnostics=false

diff --git a/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaRegionReadDiagnostics.java b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaRegionReadDiagnostics.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..27adb4b0bbf99660b67e1f0d6fbf9d9e77b520cc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaRegionReadDiagnostics.java
@@ -0,0 +1,65 @@
+package fun.bm.lophinya.compat;
+
+import ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.common.util.TickThread;
+import net.minecraft.core.BlockPos;
+import net.minecraft.world.level.Level;
+
+/**
+ * Lophinya: makes an off-region block read fail the way every other ownership violation fails.
+ *
+ * <h2>The gap</h2>
+ * {@code Level#getCurrentWorldData()} returns {@code null} when the calling thread is not ticking a
+ * region of that world - a global-region task, an async thread, the server thread. Folia's
+ * {@code Level#getBlockStateIfLoaded} dereferences it with no null check, so a cross-region block
+ * read does not end in {@code TickThread.ensureTickThread}'s message (which carries the thread
+ * context, the world and the position, and logs a stack trace). It ends in:
+ *
+ * <pre>
+ *   NullPointerException: Cannot read field "captureTreeGeneration"
+ *     because the return value of "Level.getCurrentWorldData()" is null
+ * </pre>
+ *
+ * <p>That names a field which has nothing to do with the problem, and nothing else. Measured: 26 of
+ * them in one soak run, all from {@code CraftWorld#rayTraceBlocks} called off-region. Working out
+ * what they meant took a separate investigation, and a probe run was written off as "some plugin ray
+ * traced my armour stand" because the exception could not be read.
+ *
+ * <h2>Why this matters here specifically</h2>
+ * This fork's whole model is "let it load, then fail loudly at the real callsite" - which only works
+ * if the failure can be attributed. An unattributable NPE is the one failure mode the model cannot
+ * absorb.
+ *
+ * <h2>What this changes</h2>
+ * Nothing about the outcome. The read already fails and still fails, with the same
+ * {@code RuntimeException}-ness, at the same place, for the same reason. It changes the exception's
+ * <i>identity</i> from an NPE about a random field into the platform's own ownership error, and adds
+ * the stack trace and context that error already logs. This is the same "pure diagnostics" category
+ * as patch 0024's runtime access guard.
+ *
+ * <p>If {@code ensureTickThread} unexpectedly does not throw - the thread does own the position but
+ * has no world data, which should not be reachable - the caller falls through to the original NPE.
+ * Diagnostics must not invent a new outcome.
+ *
+ * <h2>Scope</h2>
+ * Only {@code getBlockStateIfLoaded}, the one path with measured evidence. Other
+ * {@code getCurrentWorldData()} dereferences have the same shape but no observed occurrence yet, and
+ * a blanket sweep of them would be a behaviour change dressed as a diagnostic.
+ *
+ * <p>Kill switch: {@code -Dlophinya.compat.regionReadDiagnostics=false} restores the bare NPE.
+ */
+public final class LophinyaRegionReadDiagnostics {
+
+    public static final boolean ENABLED =
+        !"false".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("lophinya.compat.regionReadDiagnostics", "true"));
+
+    private LophinyaRegionReadDiagnostics() {
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Throws the platform's ownership error if this thread has no regionized world data for
+     * {@code level}. Called only when the data is already known to be null.
+     */
+    public static void reportMissingWorldData(final Level level, final BlockPos pos) {
+        TickThread.ensureTickThread(level, pos, "Cannot read block state off-region");
+    }
+}
